    "text": "A particle of specific charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">q</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>kg</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is projected from the origin towards positive x-axis with a velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> in a uniform magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mover><mtext>k</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. The velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;of the particle after time&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> will be (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)",
